   "subject": "Re: Warning message",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The first issue is not necessarily problematic, though it does indicate some numerical instabilities as the EM should always be increasing. The second issue is more serious as it indicates the likelihood is flat at the MLE location, so the estimates you are seeing are not particularly reliable given how exchangeable the parameter estimates are.<div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
